{"parentUuid":"62bca932-6444-4b00-bb79-929a8658f2fa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLMdS5qpPvFRZMg4eLFV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm finishing the last follow-up from the #752 review, a bounded shutdown after a signal. The test passes and fails without the bound, and I'm reapplying the source change my revert undid before committing.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2677,"cache_read_input_tokens":360893,"output_tokens":1349,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":49},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2677,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":360893,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2677},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLMdRsgbX6Gy2GjkKKHs","requestRef":"b76fb546-38c0-44b2-a1b2-499541e7e493","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"1e172a19-3c98-4550-ba41-8b5181b21932","timestamp":"2026-11-23T18:46:11.376Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"1e172a19-3c98-4550-ba41-8b5181b21932","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLMdS5qpPvFRZMg4eLFV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RN8YyXdjm8yJJw6AnivbjU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/acpfu && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='cli/src/acp_stdio.ts'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''  const stop = (code: number) => { void server.close().finally(() => process.exit(code)); };\n'''\nnew='''  // close() waits for every session to stop. A session that never does must not keep a signalled process alive.\n  const stop = (code: number) => {\n    setTimeout(() => process.exit(code), options.shutdownGraceMs ?? ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS).unref();\n    void server.close().finally(() => process.exit(code));\n  };\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''  isDirectory?: (value: string) => boolean;\n}'''\nnew='''  isDirectory?: (value: string) => boolean;\n  /** How long a signalled process waits for its sessions to stop before it exits anyway. */\n  shutdownGraceMs?: number;\n}\n\nconst ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS = 10_000;'''\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .; echo \"tsc $?\"; HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 250 node --import tsx --test test/acp_review_fixes.test.ts 2>&1 | rtk proxy grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail) \"; cd .. && git status --short && git add cli/src/acp_stdio.ts cli/test/acp_review_fixes.test.ts && git commit -q -m \"fix(acp): bound shutdown after a signal\n\nclose() waits for every session to stop, with no upper bound, so a session\nstuck while stopping kept a signalled adapter alive. The process now exits\nwith the signal's status after 10 s at the latest. Follow-up from the review\nof the adapter fixes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/acp-shutdown-bound 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/acp-shutdown-bound --title \"fix(acp): bound shutdown after a signal\" --body \"Follow-up from the review of #752.\n\n\\`close()\\` waits for every session's sidecar to stop and has no upper bound, so a session stuck while stopping kept a signalled \\`nexus acp\\` alive. A signal now also starts a 10 s timer that exits with the signal's status (143 or 130) if the sessions have not stopped by then.\n\nTest: a child process runs the adapter with a sidecar whose shutdown never resolves and a 500 ms grace; SIGTERM must end it with 143. The test fails with the timer removed. \\`acp_review_fixes.test.ts\\`: 7 pass locally (Node 24); \\`tsc --noEmit\\` clean.\n\nThe review's other follow-up (the \\\"still stopping\\\" guard cleared only by a turn result) is already handled on the release branch: the guard also clears when the sidecar reports the session idle.\n\nReference coding: exempt (small fix specified by a review finding).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1","description":"Reapply the shutdown bound, retest, commit, push and open the PR","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2677,"cache_read_input_tokens":360893,"output_tokens":1349,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":49},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2677,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":360893,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2677},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":8453,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RN8YyXdjm8yJJw6AnivbjU":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/acpfu && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='cli/src/acp_stdio.ts'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''  const stop = (code: number) => { void server.close().finally(() => process.exit(code)); };\n'''\nnew='''  // close() waits for every session to stop. A session that never does must not keep a signalled process alive.\n  const stop = (code: number) => {\n    setTimeout(() => process.exit(code), options.shutdownGraceMs ?? ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS).unref();\n    void server.close().finally(() => process.exit(code));\n  };\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''  isDirectory?: (value: string) => boolean;\n}'''\nnew='''  isDirectory?: (value: string) => boolean;\n  /** How long a signalled process waits for its sessions to stop before it exits anyway. */\n  shutdownGraceMs?: number;\n}\n\nconst ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS = 10_000;'''\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .; echo \"tsc $?\"; HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 250 node --import tsx --test test/acp_review_fixes.test.ts 2>&1 | rtk proxy grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail) \"; cd .. && git status --short && git add cli/src/acp_stdio.ts cli/test/acp_review_fixes.test.ts && git commit -q -m \"fix(acp): bound shutdown after a signal\n\nclose() waits for every session to stop, with no upper bound, so a session\nstuck while stopping kept a signalled adapter alive. The process now exits\nwith the signal's status after 10 s at the latest. Follow-up from the review\nof the adapter fixes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/acp-shutdown-bound 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/acp-shutdown-bound --title \"fix(acp): bound shutdown after a signal\" --body \"Follow-up from the review of #752.\n\n\\`close()\\` waits for every session's sidecar to stop and has no upper bound, so a session stuck while stopping kept a signalled \\`nexus acp\\` alive. A signal now also starts a 10 s timer that exits with the signal's status (143 or 130) if the sessions have not stopped by then.\n\nTest: a child process runs the adapter with a sidecar whose shutdown never resolves and a 500 ms grace; SIGTERM must end it with 143. The test fails with the timer removed. \\`acp_review_fixes.test.ts\\`: 7 pass locally (Node 24); \\`tsc --noEmit\\` clean.\n\nThe review's other follow-up (the \\\"still stopping\\\" guard cleared only by a turn result) is already handled on the release branch: the guard also clears when the sidecar reports the session idle.\n\nReference coding: exempt (small fix specified by a review finding).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1","description":"Reapply the shutdown bound, retest, commit, push and open the PR","timeout":400000}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChLMdRsgbX6Gy2GjkKKHs","requestRef":"b76fb546-38c0-44b2-a1b2-499541e7e493","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f5abaa6-e3c2-498e-898a-84654baf1866","timestamp":"2026-11-23T18:46:19.935Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
