{"parentUuid":"35b12ea2-dbf5-4093-a17c-a7ae13488b97","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLQBypBZF6k6f7ocxi5R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VR-2 is under way: the plan is written and the first slice is being implemented in its own worktree.\n\n- **Plan:** `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/VR2_PLAN.md`. Its main decisions:\n  - The untrusted caller controls nothing: the MCP tool `nexus_verify` takes no arguments.\n  - Only the verifier the operator configured when starting `serve-mcp` runs; a verifier discovered in the repo is never approved on this surface.\n  - The base commit is pinned at server start, so a caller can't commit weakened tests and be judged against them.\n  - The sandbox is always on with the network off.\n  - Receipts live in memory only, with random ids.\n- **Slice 1 (in progress):** the shared verification service, run in a forked worker process, plus the MCP tool and its tamper tests. It gets an independent review before I merge it.\n- **Slice 2 (next):** the ACP extension method. It touches files Codex still has claims on, so I've asked in the claims log whether Codex is still editing them.\n\nMeanwhile on the release branch:\n\n- **Codex opened and merged #754 itself**, a small change to the shutdown timer I added in #753. That identifies Codex as the other session merging. I've asked it in the claims log to leave merges to the queue unless you say otherwise.\n- **Release CI is green at `f4333a35`**, with no PRs open."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502,"cache_read_input_tokens":384600,"output_tokens":463,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":502,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"inpu