{"parentUuid":"85a550e2-3e19-4c88-861c-6a4949595a47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLTQXPfG6tvcZG2txmBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VR-2 slice 1 is implemented, committed and pushed (16 new tests pass, type check clean). I'm opening the PR now and sending it for independent review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":396790,"output_tokens":4998,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4998,"cache_read_input_tokens":396790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLTQXBktttFLCfyoKHXE","requestRef":"daed1088-307e-49be-85a6-1d97545602d9","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9d28bcc9-ec99-4a6e-a30e-7219ed7bc00b","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:01:55.569Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"9d28bcc9-ec99-4a6e-a30e-7219ed7bc00b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLTQXPfG6tvcZG2txmBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QLxiznJg8q79ph2ugDiCgX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vr2.md","content":"## What this adds\n\n`nexus serve-mcp` gains a tool, `nexus_verify`, that lets another harness ask Nexus to check the change in the served workspace and get back a verdict and a receipt id (plan unit VR-2, decision D20 at its default). This is slice 1 of three; the ACP extension and the evidence document follow.\n\n## What the caller controls: nothing\n\nThe MCP caller is untrusted.\n\n- The tool takes no arguments. Any argument (a verifier command, a path, a claimed outcome, an extra field) is rejected with `-32602` and nothing runs.\n- Only the verifier the operator named when starting the server runs (`--authoritative-verifier`, with `--deliverable-file` for deliverables). A verifier discovered in the repository is never approved on this surface: the result is BLOCKED / `VERIFIER_NOT_APPROVED` with nothing executed, and the caller is never prompted.\n- The base commit is pinned when the server starts. A weakened test committed afterwards is judged against the pinned base, not accepted as the new baseline.\n- The sandbox is always on with the network off. The call is refused in read-only mode, where managed policy requires a human for command execution, and in a workspace with no commit.\n- Every verdict, BLOCKED included, is a successful result with a receipt. An error comes back only when no verdict exists.\n\n## How it runs\n\n- `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts` calls the existing `verifyChange` in a forked worker (`verify_worker.ts`). `verify.ts` and the v3 result schema are unchanged: there is no second verification path.\n- One verification at a time per process, not queued. A watchdog and `notifications/cancelled` end the worker and its children; output is capped.\n- Receipts: `vr-` plus 32 random hex digits, in memory only (32 at most, oldest evicted), with the SHA-256 of the document. Read back through `resources/read nexus://verify-receipt/<id>`. There is no file store, because the caller can already write any file the server's user can.\n\n## Tests (16 new)\n\n`mcp_verify.test.ts` (6, over real stdio) and `verify_service.test.ts` (10): verdict and receipt for a good change; a weakened test and a broken product are not VERIFIED; 23 hostile argument shapes are refused with nothing run; an unapproved discovered verifier runs nothing; a weakened test committed after the pin is blocked; the refusals; single flight; timeout and cancellation leave no worker, no verifier child and no scratch directory; receipt ids, eviction, forged ids, byte-identical re-reads.\n\nRun locally on Node 24: both files 5 of 5 in sequence and 4 of 4 concurrently. Existing files unchanged in result: `mcp` 4, `mcp_http_delivery` 6, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `verify_command` 18, `verify_hostile` 46, `verify_sandbox` 10, `verify_schema` 4, `check_requirements` 28, `context_convergence` 57. `tsc --noEmit`, `check_invariants.mjs` and `check_requirements.mjs` pass. Node 22 has not been run locally; CI covers it.\n\n## Limits, stated plainly\n\n- The guarantee covers the request. A caller that can run commands as the server's user (and `serve-mcp` already offers `run_command`) can still tamper with `node_modules`, git configuration or the Nexus installation. Only OS isolation prevents that; the docs say so.\n- A commit made before the server starts becomes the base. Start the server at the commit you want changes judged against.\n- If the server is killed with SIGKILL, the worker stops only when its current verifier run ends.\n\n## Deviations from the plan\n\n- Timeout and cancel signal the worker's whole process tree by pid, not only its process group: the verifier runs under `timeout`, which leaves the group.\n- `harness.test.ts` is not edited (another agent holds it); the equivalent assertion is in `mcp_verify.test.ts`.\n- In `cli/src/index.ts` only the `serve-mcp` command changed.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was queried: no corpus project exposes verification as an MCP tool or an ACP extension. The plan (`VR2_PLAN.md`, reference-coding section) records the queries; the tool's refusal of all arguments follows from this repo's own VR-1 hardening rather than from a peer.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":396790,"output_tokens":4998,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4998,"cache_read_input_tokens":396790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":14708,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QLxiznJg8q79ph2ugDiCgX":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vr2.md","content":"## What this adds\n\n`nexus serve-mcp` gains a tool, `nexus_verify`, that lets another harness ask Nexus to check the change in the served workspace and get back a verdict and a receipt id (plan unit VR-2, decision D20 at its default). This is slice 1 of three; the ACP extension and the evidence document follow.\n\n## What the caller controls: nothing\n\nThe MCP caller is untrusted.\n\n- The tool takes no arguments. Any argument (a verifier command, a path, a claimed outcome, an extra field) is rejected with `-32602` and nothing runs.\n- Only the verifier the operator named when starting the server runs (`--authoritative-verifier`, with `--deliverable-file` for deliverables). A verifier discovered in the repository is never approved on this surface: the result is BLOCKED / `VERIFIER_NOT_APPROVED` with nothing executed, and the caller is never prompted.\n- The base commit is pinned when the server starts. A weakened test committed afterwards is judged against the pinned base, not accepted as the new baseline.\n- The sandbox is always on with the network off. The call is refused in read-only mode, where managed policy requires a human for command execution, and in a workspace with no commit.\n- Every verdict, BLOCKED included, is a successful result with a receipt. An error comes back only when no verdict exists.\n\n## How it runs\n\n- `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts` calls the existing `verifyChange` in a forked worker (`verify_worker.ts`). `verify.ts` and the v3 result schema are unchanged: there is no second verification path.\n- One verification at a time per process, not queued. A watchdog and `notifications/cancelled` end the worker and its children; output is capped.\n- Receipts: `vr-` plus 32 random hex digits, in memory only (32 at most, oldest evicted), with the SHA-256 of the document. Read back through `resources/read nexus://verify-receipt/<id>`. There is no file store, because the caller can already write any file the server's user can.\n\n## Tests (16 new)\n\n`mcp_verify.test.ts` (6, over real stdio) and `verify_service.test.ts` (10): verdict and receipt for a good change; a weakened test and a broken product are not VERIFIED; 23 hostile argument shapes are refused with nothing run; an unapproved discovered verifier runs nothing; a weakened test committed after the pin is blocked; the refusals; single flight; timeout and cancellation leave no worker, no verifier child and no scratch directory; receipt ids, eviction, forged ids, byte-identical re-reads.\n\nRun locally on Node 24: both files 5 of 5 in sequence and 4 of 4 concurrently. Existing files unchanged in result: `mcp` 4, `mcp_http_delivery` 6, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `verify_command` 18, `verify_hostile` 46, `verify_sandbox` 10, `verify_schema` 4, `check_requirements` 28, `context_convergence` 57. `tsc --noEmit`, `check_invariants.mjs` and `check_requirements.mjs` pass. Node 22 has not been run locally; CI covers it.\n\n## Limits, stated plainly\n\n- The guarantee covers the request. A caller that can run commands as the server's user (and `serve-mcp` already offers `run_command`) can still tamper with `node_modules`, git configuration or the Nexus installation. Only OS isolation prevents that; the docs say so.\n- A commit made before the server starts becomes the base. Start the server at the commit you want changes judged against.\n- If the server is killed with SIGKILL, the worker stops only when its current verifier run ends.\n\n## Deviations from the plan\n\n- Timeout and cancel signal the worker's whole process tree by pid, not only its process group: the verifier runs under `timeout`, which leaves the group.\n- `harness.test.ts` is not edited (another agent holds it); the equivalent assertion is in `mcp_verify.test.ts`.\n- In `cli/src/index.ts` only the `serve-mcp` command changed.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was queried: no corpus project exposes verification as an MCP tool or an ACP extension. The plan (`VR2_PLAN.md`, reference-coding section) records the queries; the tool's refusal of all arguments follows from this repo's own VR-1 hardening rather than from a peer.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLTQXBktttFLCfyoKHXE","requestRef":"daed1088-307e-49be-85a6-1d97545602d9","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uu