 do not add a duplicate CI job. Keep Rust warnings scoped and justified rather than inventing a large analyzer bundle. Add complexity reporting or thresholds only for critical high-change functions after measuring the baseline; avoid arbitrary whole-repos\n+**Progress (2026-11-23, `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`):** The Clippy CI gate proposed above is already implemented through `make lint` (`Makefile:24-27`), which runs CLI typecheck, Clippy with `-D warnings`, and diff-scoped rustfmt. CI calls this target in `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64` (`.github/workflows/\n-**Required tests / acceptance:** CI runs Clippy on exact PR merge head; seeded warning fails. TypeScript strict build is verified on Node 22 and 24. A changed critical function crossing an agreed CC/nesting threshold requires review or decomposition. Workflow is protected by WP-P10-01.\n+**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing exact-main CI evidence demonstrates the static gate passes on `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`; the same gate is required in the PR workflow. A changed critical function crossing an agreed, baseline-derived CC/nesting threshold fails a focused check. The verification policy remains exposed to single-user w\n-1. **WP-P10-01** governance/acceptance authority (P0).\n-2. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\n-3. **WP-P10-03** durable evidence and candidate/policy binding (P1; can start schema design in parallel after WP-P10-01).\n-4. **WP-P10-04** aggregate resource admission and cleanup (P1; budget counters feed this work).\n-5. **WP-P10-05** static-analysis/complexity gate (P2; protected by WP-P10-01).\n+1. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\n+2. **WP-P10-03** durable evidence and candidate/policy binding (P1; implement local integrity controls and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n+3. **WP-P10-04** aggregate resource admission and cleanup (P1; budget counters feed this work).\n+4. **WP-P10-05** static-analysis/complexity gate (P2; reuse existing CI gates and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n+5. **WP-P10-01** remains deferred until a second independent maintainer is available; it is not a prerequisite for the work above or publication.\n-Each package lands independently with its own negative tests. CI green on a PR is not proof the implementation is correct; hosted checks must be tied to the exact candidate and accepted under the protected review policy.\n+Each implementable package lands independently with its own negative tests. CI green on a PR is not proof the implementation is correct; hosted checks must be tied to the exact candidate and reported alongside the single-maintainer review limitation.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e6d1a32f-3951-45f1-9f14-67dbf5ead51c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
