{"parentUuid":"b1de1369-8280-47fd-bf6a-789fa8805626","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLVQSD6i7fomzPfKqYMc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1824,"cache_read_input_tokens":417303,"output_tokens":2172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":644},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1824,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":417303,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1824},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6913,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLVQS1h9YALyyjFdKGfb","requestRef":"114c349b-b7cf-49a4-8af7-20ef2f85c60a","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c1dd3d4-9132-4985-a947-51df02002bb9","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:28:14.334Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"9c1dd3d4-9132-4985-a947-51df02002bb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLVQSD6i7fomzPfKqYMc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ReHwRXkNvF7oS4ZyAXp8Fz","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aa6055acd1b6e26f5","summary":"Apply review follow-ups to VR-2 slice 1","message":"Follow-up work on VR-2 slice 1 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2 after the independent review (your work was committed as 9b… then merged with the release branch; HEAD is 4196a306; start from the current worktree state, do not commit or push). Same working rules as before. Apply these four changes and report (under 250 words) with test results:\n\n1. SIGTERM/SIGINT must not orphan the verifier (confirmed defect: after SIGTERM of `serve-mcp` mid-verification, the verifier's `sleep`/`bwrap` survived and `nexus-verify-*` / `nexus-verifier-*` scratch dirs remained; `process.once(\"exit\")` does not fire on signal death). Add signal handling for the stdio server: on SIGTERM and SIGINT, abort the running verification, wait until it has settled (worker and descendants gone, scratch removed), shut the bridge down, then `process.exit(143|130)`. Add a small awaitable on `VerifyService` for \"abort and wait until nothing is running\" rather than polling from mcp.ts if that is cleaner. Bound the wait with a hard-exit timer (kill grace + a few seconds) that is NOT unref'd. Register the handlers only in `startStdio` (not in the constructor), so tests that construct `McpServer` in-process are unaffected, and remove nothing that the stdin-EOF path does today. Test in `cli/test/mcp_verify.test.ts`: real server over stdio with a verifier that ignores SIGTERM and sleeps; call `nexus_verify`; once the verifier is running send SIGTERM to the server; assert the server exits (143) within a bound, the verifier process and any bwrap child are gone, and no scratch dir is left. Confirm the test fails without the handler.\n\n2. In `startStdio`, the un-awaited `void this.handleMessage(req).then(...)` for the verify call has no `.catch`: a throw would be an unhandled rejection. Add a catch that writes a JSON-RPC error (-32603, with the request id) and never crashes the server.\n\n3. Read-only must be honoured however it was selected. Today `readOnly` for the verify tool is set only from `--read-only` / `--mode read-only` in the `serve-mcp` action. Also refuse when the effective configuration is read-only through the environment or config file (`REDACTED`, and whatever else `buildConfig`/`loadConfig` in `cli/src/config.ts` resolves to `approvalMode === \"read-only\"` or `readOnly`). Derive it from the same resolution the rest of the CLI uses (see how the `acp` command in `cli/src/index.ts` calls `buildConfig(program.opts())`), still editing only the `serve-mcp` command in index.ts. Add a test case to the existing refusals test: `REDACTED` in the server's env → `nexus_verify` is refused with no receipt. Make sure starting `serve-mcp` in an empty HOME with no model configured still works.\n\n4. Docs, `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` \"What this does not protect against\": make the list complete and honest. Add: the server user's HOME (`~/.config/nexus/config.env` operator settings such as verifier environment passthrough, and any user-tier managed policy) can be edited by a client that runs commands as that user; an operator verifier script or binaries on PATH outside the workspace are equally writable by that user; a receipt's verifier output tail and paths are not secret from the client (it carries the workspace path and the verifier's output, as the CLI prints); and if the server is killed with SIGKILL the verifier runs on until its own timeout and scratch directories remain (SIGTERM/SIGINT now clean up). Update the `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` line only if it now says something untrue.\n\nThen re-run: `test/mcp_verify.test.ts` 3 times in a row, `test/verify_service.test.ts` once, `test/mcp.test.ts`, `tsc --noEmit`, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`. Report file:line of each change, the test names added, pass/fail counts, and anything you could not do.","type":"message","recipient":"aa6055acd1b6e26f5","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Follow-up work on VR-2 slice 1 in /home/mike/nexu…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1824,"cache_read_input_tokens":417303,"output_tokens":2172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":644},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1824,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":417303,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1824},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15568,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ReHwRXkNvF7oS4ZyAXp8Fz":{"to":"aa6055acd1b6e26f5","summary":"Apply review follow-ups to VR-2 slice 1","message":"Follow-up work on VR-2 slice 1 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2 after the independent review (your work was committed as 9b… then merged with the release branch; HEAD is 4196a306; start from the current worktree state, do not commit or push). Same working rules as before. Apply these four changes and report (under 250 words) with test results:\n\n1. SIGTERM/SIGINT must not orphan the verifier (confirmed defect: after SIGTERM of `serve-mcp` mid-verification, the verifier's `sleep`/`bwrap` survived and `nexus-verify-*` / `nexus-verifier-*` scratch dirs remained; `process.once(\"exit\")` does not fire on signal death). Add signal handling for the stdio server: on SIGTERM and SIGINT, abort the running verification, wait until it has settled (worker and descendants gone, scratch removed), shut the bridge down, then `process.exit(143|130)`. Add a small awaitable on `VerifyService` for \"abort and wait until nothing is running\" rather than polling from mcp.ts if that is cleaner. Bound the wait with a hard-exit timer (kill grace + a few seconds) that is NOT unref'd. Register the handlers only in `startStdio` (not in the constructor), so tests that construct `McpServer` in-process are unaffected, and remove nothing that the stdin-EOF path does today. Test in `cli/test/mcp_verify.test.ts`: real server over stdio with a verifier that ignores SIGTERM and sleeps; call `nexus_verify`; once the verifier is running send SIGTERM to the server; assert the server exits (143) within a bound, the verifier process and any bwrap child are gone, and no scratch dir is left. Confirm the test fails without the handler.\n\n2. In `startStdio`, the un-awaited `void this.handleMessage(req).then(...)` for the verify call has no `.catch`: a throw would be an unhandled rejection. Add a catch that writes a JSON-RPC error (-32603, with the request id) and never crashes the server.\n\n3. Read-only must be honoured however it was selected. Today `readOnly` for the verify tool is set only from `--read-only` / `--mode read-only` in the `serve-mcp` action. Also refuse when the effective configuration is read-only through the environment or config file (`REDACTED`, and whatever else `buildConfig`/`loadConfig` in `cli/src/config.ts` resolves to `approvalMode === \"read-only\"` or `readOnly`). Derive it from the same resolution the rest of the CLI uses (see how the `acp` command in `cli/src/index.ts` calls `buildConfig(program.opts())`), still editing only the `serve-mcp` command in index.ts. Add a test case to the existing refusals test: `REDACTED` in the server's env → `nexus_verify` is refused with no receipt. Make sure starting `serve-mcp` in an empty HOME with no model configured still works.\n\n4. Docs, `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` \"What this does not protect against\": make the list complete and honest. Add: the server user's HOME (`~/.config/nexus/config.env` operator settings such as verifier environment passthrough, and any user-tier managed policy) can be edited by a client that runs commands as that user; an operator verifier script or binaries on PATH outside the workspace are equally writable by that user; a receipt's verifier output tail and paths are not secret from the client (it carries the workspace path and the verifier's output, as the CLI prints); and if the server is killed with SIGKILL the verifier runs on until its own timeout and scratch directories remain (SIGTERM/SIGINT now clean up). Update the `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` line only if it now says something untrue.\n\nThen re-run: `test/mcp_verify.test.ts` 3 times in a row, `test/verify_service.test.ts` once, `test/mcp.test.ts`, `tsc --noEmit`, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`. Report file:line of each change, the test names added, pass/fail counts, and anything you could not do."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLVQS1h9YALyyjFdKGfb","requestRef":"114c349b-b7cf-49a4-8af7-20ef2f85c60a","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"928cbdf3-86ad-4932-8e41-c37ee922470d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:28:29.923Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
