{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:41:20.377Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa6055acd1b6e26f5</task-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/aa6055acd1b6e26f5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement VR-2 slice 1\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All four follow-up changes are applied in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2` (uncommitted), and every requested re-run passes.\n\n## Changes\n1. **Signals** — `cli/src/mcp.ts:996-1011`: SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers registered in `startStdio` only. They await `VerifyService.stop()`, shut the bridge down, then `process.exit(130|143)`. The hard-exit timer is kill grace + 5 s and is not unref'd.\n   - `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts:383`: new `stop()` (abort and wait until settled), backed by `settled` at `:229`.\n   - `verify_service.ts:185`: after the grace, the verifier is SIGKILLed first and the worker spared so it still removes its scratch trees; the worker is killed after a second grace.\n2. **Catch** — `cli/src/mcp.ts:969`: the un-awaited verify call now writes a `-32603` error with the request id.\n3. **Read-only** — `cli/src/index.ts:1213-1222` (inside `serve-mcp`): `readOnly` now comes from `buildConfig(options)`. An empty HOME with no model still starts (every test server runs that way).\n4. **Docs** — `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md:136-144` rewritten with the four additions; line 128 now names `REDACTED`. `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` is unchanged (still true).\n\n## Tests added (`cli/test/mcp_verify.test.ts`)\n- `:293` \"SIGTERM to the server stops a verifier that ignores SIGTERM and removes the scratch trees before the server exits\". With the handlers removed it fails (runs to its 180 s limit).\n- `:336` a `REDACTED` case in the refusals test.\n\n## Results\n- `mcp_verify`: 7 pass, 0 fail, three runs in a row.\n- `verify_service`: 10/0. `mcp.test.ts`: 4/0.\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `check_invariants.mjs` exits 0.\n\n## Caveats\n- If `buildConfig` throws, the server still starts and `nexus_verify` is refused as read-only, with a stderr notice; exiting 2 there would have broken startup for existing users with an unrelated config error.\n- The SIGKILL stage is not exercised by any test: under bubblewrap the sandbox dies on SIGTERM even when the verifier traps it, so the test exits in about 7 s on the graceful path.\n- The catch at `mcp.ts:969` has no test.\n- Node 22 was not run.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>245902</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>770001</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
